{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>For, etc.</b> Its sense: for you thought that I would requite you evil even though you return to Me; therefore My thoughts are not like your thoughts, for in My thoughts is to do good to you. And likewise: neither are your ways My ways, for My ways are upright. It is also spelled out in the book of Ezekiel that My ways are not conceivable (Ezekiel 18:29)."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 55, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:59:40.270670812Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}